1
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:04,540
You're here.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:07,380
Your organs are failing.

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,300
And your death is drawing near.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:13,440
But if you bribe the right politicians in the right order at the right time,

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,600
you can trade the nuclear warheads for medicine.

6
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,080
And it's not even a crime.

7
00:01:39,984 --> 00:01:41,044
Peace Dividend

8
00:01:42,044 --> 00:01:46,704
Your government spends more on camouflage paint than on curing Alzheimer's.

9
00:01:46,924 --> 00:01:49,464
Move one percent of the bomb budget to medicine:

10
00:01:49,464 --> 00:01:54,657
twenty-seven point two billion dollars for clinical trials, plus one hundred

11
00:01:54,657 --> 00:01:58,464
and fourteen billion dollars saved by slightly fewer explosions.

12
00:01:59,104 --> 00:02:03,344
The worst-case scenario is still the largest increase in medical research

13
00:02:03,344 --> 00:02:04,144
in history.

14
00:02:04,144 --> 00:02:08,104
Here's what one percent less murder money buys you.

15
00:02:08,604 --> 00:02:14,326
The one percent Treaty Fund gets twenty-seven point two billion dollars

16
00:02:14,326 --> 00:02:18,404
to subsidize hyper-efficient pragmatic clinical trials.

17
00:02:19,044 --> 00:02:23,924
The world saves one hundred and fourteen billion dollars it would have spent

18
00:02:23,924 --> 00:02:29,184
rebuilding bombed hospitals, treating shrapnel wounds, and housing refugees.

19
00:02:29,804 --> 00:02:34,784
Your lifetime tab for wars in countries you can't find on a map:

20
00:02:34,784 --> 00:02:40,804
one hundred and thirteen thousand, five hundred and fifty-one dollars per

21
00:02:40,804 --> 00:02:43,024
person over eighty years.

22
00:02:43,684 --> 00:02:44,744
That's per person.

23
00:02:45,443 --> 00:02:46,824
Every person on Earth.

24
00:02:47,384 --> 00:02:48,144
Including you.

25
00:02:49,004 --> 00:02:53,436
You personally have been billed one hundred and thirteen thousand, five

26
00:02:53,436 --> 00:02:58,904
hundred and fifty-one dollars for explosions on the other side of the planet,

27
00:02:58,904 --> 00:03:03,084
and nobody sent you an invoice because they knew you'd cancel.

28
00:03:04,224 --> 00:03:07,904
How one percent Less Violence Pays For Everything.

29
00:03:08,784 --> 00:03:11,924
An analysis of a decentralized F.D.A.

30
00:03:11,924 --> 00:03:18,044
shows pragmatic clinical trials can be forty-four point one times

31
00:03:18,044 --> 00:03:18,904
more efficient.

32
00:03:18,904 --> 00:03:23,284
Two ways you profit from building one percent fewer bombs:

33
00:03:23,884 --> 00:03:24,864
The Captured Money:

34
00:03:24,864 --> 00:03:28,184
twenty-seven point two billion dollars per year.

35
00:03:29,104 --> 00:03:34,604
Your governments spend two point seven two trillion dollars yearly on things

36
00:03:34,604 --> 00:03:38,604
whose sole purpose is making other things stop existing.

37
00:03:38,604 --> 00:03:41,116
Redirect one percent:

38
00:03:41,116 --> 00:03:47,346
Two point seven two trillion dollars multiplied by point zero one

39
00:03:47,346 --> 00:03:50,743
equals twenty-seven point two billion dollars.

40
00:03:50,743 --> 00:03:53,504
The rounding error on your murder budget.

41
00:03:54,304 --> 00:03:55,244
The Bonus Savings:

42
00:03:55,244 --> 00:03:59,144
one hundred and fourteen billion dollars per year.

43
00:03:59,144 --> 00:04:03,644
Wars cost eleven point four trillion dollars per year.

44
00:04:04,044 --> 00:04:10,510
Build one percent fewer bombs, fight one percent fewer wars, save one hundred

45
00:04:10,510 --> 00:04:12,564
and fourteen billion dollars.

46
00:04:12,564 --> 00:04:18,378
Eleven point four trillion dollars multiplied by point zero one equals one

47
00:04:18,378 --> 00:04:21,264
hundred and fourteen billion dollars.

48
00:04:21,944 --> 00:04:26,304
Money no longer spent on unblowing-up hospitals and bridges,

49
00:04:26,904 --> 00:04:30,144
removing shrapnel from people you put shrapnel into,

50
00:04:30,824 --> 00:04:35,464
housing refugees whose homes you converted into craters, and routing shipping

51
00:04:35,464 --> 00:04:37,284
containers around minefields.

52
00:04:38,184 --> 00:04:44,084
Your species has an entire industry dedicated to rebuilding things it blew

53
00:04:44,084 --> 00:04:44,584
up.

54
00:04:44,904 --> 00:04:49,764
You employ people to fill holes that you employed other people to make.

55
00:04:49,764 --> 00:04:55,044
On Wishonia, this is used as a children's fable about inefficiency.

56
00:04:55,764 --> 00:04:56,624
The children laugh.

57
00:04:56,904 --> 00:04:58,124
Then they ask if it's real.

58
00:04:58,584 --> 00:04:59,564
Then they stop laughing.

59
00:05:00,084 --> 00:05:04,244
It replaced the previous worst children's fable, which was about a species

60
00:05:04,244 --> 00:05:08,964
that invented an instrument called "the recorder" and then made every child

61
00:05:08,964 --> 00:05:09,664
play it.

62
00:05:10,064 --> 00:05:13,984
The violence fable is considered more tragic, but only slightly.

63
00:05:13,984 --> 00:05:19,084
Where the one hundred and fourteen billion dollars Comes From.

64
00:05:19,084 --> 00:05:22,064
Your itemized receipt for violence.

65
00:05:22,064 --> 00:05:27,504
Direct costs are seven point six six trillion dollars per year.

66
00:05:27,504 --> 00:05:33,564
This includes military budgets (two point seven two trillion dollars), infrastructure

67
00:05:33,564 --> 00:05:38,824
you blow up and then pay to rebuild (one point eight eight trillion dollars),

68
00:05:38,824 --> 00:05:44,684
humans you break (two point four five trillion dollars), and trade routes

69
00:05:44,684 --> 00:05:49,864
you keep putting mines in (six hundred and sixteen billion dollars).

70
00:05:49,864 --> 00:05:55,264
Cutting one percent saves seventy-six point six billion dollars.

71
00:05:55,264 --> 00:05:59,563
Indirect costs are three point seven trillion dollars per year.

72
00:06:00,184 --> 00:06:04,744
This is the part your accountants pretend doesn't exist, including lost

73
00:06:04,744 --> 00:06:09,144
economic growth from pointing engineers at missiles instead of medicine

74
00:06:09,144 --> 00:06:14,224
(two point seven two trillion dollars), and veteran healthcare, because

75
00:06:14,224 --> 00:06:19,403
the humans you send to war come back needing hospitals (two hundred billion

76
00:06:19,403 --> 00:06:20,064
dollars).

77
00:06:20,064 --> 00:06:22,964
This includes refugees, P.T.S.D.,

78
00:06:23,664 --> 00:06:26,524
environmental damage, and lost human capital.

79
00:06:27,164 --> 00:06:30,764
Cutting one percent saves thirty-seven billion dollars.

80
00:06:30,764 --> 00:06:31,347
Total:

81
00:06:31,347 --> 00:06:36,024
eleven point four trillion dollars per year on war.

82
00:06:36,024 --> 00:06:41,744
One percent less war saves one hundred and fourteen billion dollars.

83
00:06:41,744 --> 00:06:44,784
On your planet, this is called "a good deal."

84
00:06:45,244 --> 00:06:50,324
On mine, it's called "so obvious that failing to do it constitutes evidence

85
00:06:50,324 --> 00:06:52,204
of a cognitive disability.".

86
00:06:52,944 --> 00:06:55,184
Plus cancer gets cured as a bonus.

87
00:06:55,824 --> 00:06:57,164
Almost forgot about that part.

88
00:06:57,164 --> 00:07:02,284
The benefits cascade beyond medicine in ways that should be obvious but

89
00:07:02,284 --> 00:07:03,304
apparently aren't.

90
00:07:04,204 --> 00:07:05,904
Addiction is a neurological disorder;

91
00:07:06,244 --> 00:07:08,944
cure the brain chemistry and the drug trade collapses.

92
00:07:09,724 --> 00:07:12,524
Most poverty is catastrophic medical costs;

93
00:07:12,884 --> 00:07:15,064
cure the diseases and people can work again.

94
00:07:16,044 --> 00:07:18,664
Radicalization is often untreated mental illness;

95
00:07:19,144 --> 00:07:23,904
you can't bomb someone into being mentally stable (you tried this, it didn't

96
00:07:23,904 --> 00:07:28,564
work, cost eight trillion dollars, created more radicals).

97
00:07:29,364 --> 00:07:31,844
Fix the biology and you fix the society.

98
00:07:32,384 --> 00:07:33,684
This is not a new insight.

99
00:07:33,884 --> 00:07:38,184
It's just one your species keeps forgetting because explosions are louder

100
00:07:38,184 --> 00:07:39,244
than pharmacology.

101
00:07:40,164 --> 00:07:41,124
The Two Numbers.

102
00:07:41,924 --> 00:07:44,884
The Captured Dividend (the money you definitely get):

103
00:07:44,884 --> 00:07:50,259
two point seven two trillion dollars in military spending times one percent

104
00:07:50,259 --> 00:07:53,824
equals twenty-seven point two billion dollars per year.

105
00:07:54,364 --> 00:07:55,344
That's a bank transfer.

106
00:07:55,724 --> 00:07:58,184
It happens because the treaty says it happens.

107
00:07:58,644 --> 00:08:00,224
No behavior change required.

108
00:08:01,024 --> 00:08:02,444
The Societal Dividend

109
00:08:03,064 --> 00:08:05,584
(money you save by being slightly less insane):

110
00:08:05,584 --> 00:08:09,304
one hundred and fourteen billion dollars per year.

111
00:08:09,744 --> 00:08:13,704
Depends on whether one percent fewer bombs means one percent fewer wars.

112
00:08:14,624 --> 00:08:15,904
The Elasticity Question.

113
00:08:15,904 --> 00:08:22,104
The elasticity parameter (e equals one point zero) asks the only interesting

114
00:08:22,104 --> 00:08:22,864
question here:

115
00:08:23,444 --> 00:08:28,384
if you cut military spending one percent, do war costs actually drop one

116
00:08:28,384 --> 00:08:29,044
percent too?

117
00:08:29,584 --> 00:08:34,064
Or do humans, being humans, find a way to keep killing each other at full

118
00:08:34,064 --> 00:08:34,564
price?

119
00:08:35,264 --> 00:08:40,004
At e equals zero point two five (the "humans are barely trainable" scenario),

120
00:08:40,644 --> 00:08:42,984
only a quarter of cuts reduce violence.

121
00:08:42,984 --> 00:08:48,124
At e equals zero point five (the "humans are somewhat rational" scenario,

122
00:08:48,684 --> 00:08:50,324
which is historically optimistic),

123
00:08:50,944 --> 00:08:52,204
half the cuts translate.

124
00:08:53,024 --> 00:08:57,144
At e equals one point zero (full match, the baseline assumption,

125
00:08:57,824 --> 00:09:02,284
probably generous given your track record), every dollar cut is a dollar

126
00:09:02,284 --> 00:09:03,644
of war cost saved.

127
00:09:04,344 --> 00:09:08,784
At e greater than one point zero, curing cancer together turns out to be

128
00:09:08,784 --> 00:09:13,324
better bonding than threatening each other with missiles, which is suspiciously

129
00:09:13,324 --> 00:09:16,144
wholesome and therefore the scenario I trust least.

130
00:09:17,004 --> 00:09:17,764
It doesn't matter.

131
00:09:18,264 --> 00:09:23,235
Even at e equals zero point two five, the Captured Dividend of twenty-seven

132
00:09:23,235 --> 00:09:27,264
point two billion dollars is treaty-mandated.

133
00:09:27,264 --> 00:09:30,944
That money moves regardless of whether you manage to be less violent.

134
00:09:31,424 --> 00:09:33,484
It's a bank transfer, not a prayer.

135
00:09:34,284 --> 00:09:36,644
The Part Where the Math Gets Embarrassing.

136
00:09:36,644 --> 00:09:42,624
The guaranteed floor is twenty-seven point two billion dollars per year.

137
00:09:42,624 --> 00:09:44,124
Direct budget transfer.

138
00:09:44,444 --> 00:09:48,744
No elasticity, no assumptions, no hoping humans behave.

139
00:09:49,244 --> 00:09:49,984
Just math.

140
00:09:50,624 --> 00:09:55,164
The best case is one hundred and fourteen billion dollars per year in total

141
00:09:55,164 --> 00:09:56,304
societal benefit;

142
00:09:56,784 --> 00:09:59,324
the range is wide because, again, your species.

143
00:10:00,264 --> 00:10:04,404
Even the pessimistic scenarios stay above roughly fifty billion dollars

144
00:10:04,404 --> 00:10:09,664
annually, which means your "worst case" is still the largest increase in

145
00:10:09,664 --> 00:10:11,984
medical research funding in human history.

146
00:10:12,663 --> 00:10:17,484
For context, the Captured Dividend alone would boost global medical research

147
00:10:17,484 --> 00:10:21,964
funding by roughly forty percent over the current sixty-seven point five

148
00:10:21,964 --> 00:10:23,663
billion dollars baseline.

149
00:10:24,404 --> 00:10:29,064
You've been spending more on camouflage paint than on curing Alzheimer's.

150
00:10:29,724 --> 00:10:30,404
Camouflage paint.

151
00:10:30,804 --> 00:10:32,204
To make things invisible.

152
00:10:32,564 --> 00:10:36,404
While Alzheimer's makes people invisible and you can't even be bothered

153
00:10:36,404 --> 00:10:37,644
to match the budget.

154
00:10:38,444 --> 00:10:40,664
What You're Assuming (and Where It Gets Shaky).

155
00:10:41,304 --> 00:10:42,024
The G.D.P.

156
00:10:42,024 --> 00:10:42,584
Multiplier.

157
00:10:43,524 --> 00:10:46,764
Spend a dollar on weapons, get sixty cents of economic value.

158
00:10:47,144 --> 00:10:50,124
Spend a dollar on healthcare, get four dollars and thirty cents back.

159
00:10:50,644 --> 00:10:52,144
Your species chose weapons.

160
00:10:52,664 --> 00:10:53,164
Every time.

161
00:10:53,464 --> 00:10:53,964
For centuries.

162
00:10:54,444 --> 00:10:56,804
On Wishonia, this would be considered evidence.

163
00:10:57,284 --> 00:11:00,884
On Earth, it is considered an anecdote, which is what humans call evidence

164
00:11:00,884 --> 00:11:02,244
when they don't want to act on it.

165
00:11:02,244 --> 00:11:06,884
The Lost Economic Growth component (two point seven two trillion dollars)

166
00:11:06,884 --> 00:11:08,304
already captures this difference.

167
00:11:08,704 --> 00:11:11,324
It's not double-counted, just consistently ignored.

168
00:11:12,024 --> 00:11:13,444
The Elasticity Assumption.

169
00:11:14,204 --> 00:11:19,084
The treaty requires multilateral cuts, so relative military balance is preserved.

170
00:11:19,564 --> 00:11:22,604
If your neighbor also cuts one percent, neither of you is weaker.

171
00:11:23,164 --> 00:11:27,184
The Societal Dividend assumes one percent less spending means one percent

172
00:11:27,184 --> 00:11:28,124
less war cost.

173
00:11:28,884 --> 00:11:29,784
Reality is messier.

174
00:11:29,784 --> 00:11:31,724
Some costs lag by years.

175
00:11:32,164 --> 00:11:34,724
Some wars are fueled by boredom rather than budgets.

176
00:11:35,024 --> 00:11:39,144
And military spending may occasionally deter a war, though it starts far

177
00:11:39,144 --> 00:11:43,124
more than it prevents (a bit like crediting your arsonist neighbor for occasionally

178
00:11:43,124 --> 00:11:44,384
calling the fire department).

179
00:11:45,084 --> 00:11:48,844
Here's why the elasticity is probably better than one point zero:

180
00:11:48,844 --> 00:11:51,284
military spending doesn't just respond to threats;

181
00:11:51,624 --> 00:11:52,704
it generates them.

182
00:11:52,704 --> 00:11:56,784
Robert Pape at the University of Chicago found that ninety-five percent

183
00:11:56,784 --> 00:12:00,244
of suicide terrorist attacks from nineteen eighty to two thousand and three

184
00:12:00,244 --> 00:12:04,684
were responses to foreign military occupation, not ideology.

185
00:12:05,444 --> 00:12:09,344
Half the attackers had no religious motivation at all (the leading group

186
00:12:09,344 --> 00:12:11,344
was atheist Marxists).

187
00:12:11,944 --> 00:12:16,104
Your eight trillion dollar War on Terror took terrorist attacks from about

188
00:12:16,104 --> 00:12:21,244
one thousand per year to nearly seventeen thousand by twenty fourteen.

189
00:12:21,244 --> 00:12:23,504
Bases provoke resistance,

190
00:12:24,344 --> 00:12:27,864
resistance justifies bigger budgets, bigger budgets fund more bases.

191
00:12:28,384 --> 00:12:31,844
It's a feedback loop, and feedback loops don't scale linearly.

192
00:12:32,424 --> 00:12:35,884
Cut one percent of the bases, you remove one percent of the provocation,

193
00:12:36,284 --> 00:12:39,504
which removes more than one percent of the terrorism, which removes the

194
00:12:39,504 --> 00:12:42,324
justification for more than one percent of next year's budget.

195
00:12:42,804 --> 00:12:46,864
The elasticity isn't one point zero because you're not just reducing spending;

196
00:12:47,284 --> 00:12:51,044
you're interrupting the cycle that manufactures the thing you're spending on.

197
00:12:51,044 --> 00:12:54,584
It's like discovering that your umbrella was causing the rain.

198
00:12:55,244 --> 00:12:57,444
(See the full data on occupation and terrorism.).

199
00:12:58,244 --> 00:12:59,964
And you've tested this at scale.

200
00:13:00,504 --> 00:13:04,524
After World War Two, America cut military spending eighty-seven point six

201
00:13:04,524 --> 00:13:09,464
percent (from one point four two trillion dollars to one hundred and seventy-six

202
00:13:09,464 --> 00:13:14,264
billion dollars in today's money) and got the greatest economic boom in

203
00:13:14,264 --> 00:13:15,344
human history:

204
00:13:15,344 --> 00:13:17,024
eight percent G.D.P.

205
00:13:17,024 --> 00:13:22,064
growth for a decade, home ownership doubled, the interstate highway system.

206
00:13:22,584 --> 00:13:26,644
The Cold War ended, spending dropped by half, and you accidentally invented

207
00:13:26,644 --> 00:13:27,224
the internet.

208
00:13:27,944 --> 00:13:30,804
Every time your species stops buying explosions,

209
00:13:31,624 --> 00:13:33,104
prosperity shows up uninvited.

210
00:13:33,524 --> 00:13:35,524
You're asking for one percent.

211
00:13:35,524 --> 00:13:39,284
You've proven you can handle eighty-seven point six percent.

212
00:13:39,284 --> 00:13:40,284
How Good Are the Sources?

213
00:13:41,044 --> 00:13:44,224
I'm being honest about confidence levels, which is more than your murder

214
00:13:44,224 --> 00:13:45,024
engineers do.

215
00:13:45,024 --> 00:13:50,224
The cost category of military spending, sourced from the Stockholm International

216
00:13:50,224 --> 00:13:53,284
Peace Research Institute, or S.I.P.R.I.

217
00:13:53,284 --> 00:13:55,324
(peer-reviewed), has high confidence.

218
00:13:56,164 --> 00:14:01,364
Infrastructure damage, sourced from Brown slash Watson Costs of War, has

219
00:14:01,364 --> 00:14:02,404
medium confidence.

220
00:14:03,324 --> 00:14:06,684
Trade disruption, from the World Bank, has medium confidence.

221
00:14:07,824 --> 00:14:10,174
Lost economic growth, based on S.I.P.R.I.

222
00:14:10,174 --> 00:14:12,444
estimates, has medium-low confidence.

223
00:14:12,444 --> 00:14:18,364
Psychological impact, from a PubMed meta-analysis, has medium confidence.

224
00:14:19,204 --> 00:14:23,524
Lost human capital, based on author estimates, has low confidence.

225
00:14:24,544 --> 00:14:25,324
The Safe Bet.

226
00:14:26,164 --> 00:14:31,208
For policy decisions, use the Captured Dividend of twenty-seven point two

227
00:14:31,208 --> 00:14:34,124
billion dollars as the reliable number.

228
00:14:34,724 --> 00:14:37,284
Money moved directly to medical research.

229
00:14:37,284 --> 00:14:40,684
No assumptions about whether humans will fight less.

230
00:14:41,224 --> 00:14:45,264
Just a bank transfer from the explosion account to the medicine account.

231
00:14:46,224 --> 00:14:50,484
The Societal Dividend is the upside if you manage to behave yourselves.

232
00:14:50,984 --> 00:14:51,964
I'm not holding my breath.

233
00:14:52,384 --> 00:14:54,524
(I don't have lungs, but the expression stands.).

234
00:14:55,624 --> 00:14:57,764
The Trajectory, Not the Snapshot.

235
00:14:59,004 --> 00:15:04,764
Skeptics ask whether one percent fewer bombs means exactly one percent fewer wars.

236
00:15:04,764 --> 00:15:06,704
This is the wrong question.

237
00:15:07,184 --> 00:15:12,084
It's like asking whether the first seed planted produced exactly one tree's

238
00:15:12,084 --> 00:15:12,744
worth of shade.

239
00:15:13,284 --> 00:15:16,904
The question is what happens when the seeds keep growing.

240
00:15:17,784 --> 00:15:23,124
Your species cut military spending eighty-seven point six percent after

241
00:15:23,124 --> 00:15:27,044
World War Two and got the greatest economic boom in history.

242
00:15:27,544 --> 00:15:29,224
That's the empirical answer.

243
00:15:29,744 --> 00:15:34,444
But even that misses the point, because the one percent treaty doesn't stay

244
00:15:34,444 --> 00:15:35,992
at one percent.

245
00:15:35,992 --> 00:15:41,384
Incentive Alignment Bonds are tradable securities held by rich and powerful

246
00:15:41,384 --> 00:15:45,364
people whose income scales directly with treaty expansion.

247
00:15:45,944 --> 00:15:50,564
At one percent, bondholder payouts are two point seven two billion dollars

248
00:15:50,564 --> 00:15:51,644
per year.

249
00:15:52,004 --> 00:15:53,664
At two percent, they double.

250
00:15:54,164 --> 00:15:57,624
At ten percent, they collect ten times as much.

251
00:15:57,624 --> 00:16:01,444
These aren't activists you can ignore at a dinner party.

